          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: चाँद",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चाँद (chā̃d) — \"the moon\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From Sanskrit चन्द्र (candra), 'shining, the moon', on a root meaning 'to glow'. The moon is named for what it does, not for what it is."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The same root surfaces in Latin candēre, 'to shine white' — which is where English gets candle, candid and incandescent. A candle and the moon are the same idea in two languages."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The second of five, and a word that means 'the shining one'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
