          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बादल (bādal) — \"a cloud\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बादल (bādal) is usually traced to a Sanskrit adjective for 'cloudy' built on वारि (vāri), 'water', though the route is less tidy than the three words before it and the sources do not all agree on the steps."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is worth marking. Three clean etymologies in a row can make the fourth look clean too, and this one is not — it is probable rather than settled, and the difference matters."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The fourth of five, and the first this chapter has had to hedge on."
            }
          ]
        },
