        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: आसमान",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आसमान (āsmān) — \"the sky\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A Persian word, āsmān, whose older Iranian form is a cousin of Sanskrit अश्मन् (aśman) — and aśman means 'stone'. The sky was imagined as a stone vault overhead."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit's own everyday word for sky, आकाश (ākāśa), is a different word from a different root, and Hindi has both. So the sky above a Hindi speaker can be a Persian stone dome or a Sanskrit open space, depending on which word is reached for."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The fifth of five. The sky is furnished."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
